+
+# 2026-10-10-v5-task-title-ownership
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-10-v5-task-title-ownership.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Advances the Session writer to V5 and adds provider task-title ownership tied to earlier confirmed registration.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-10-v5-task-title-ownership
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "SessionHeader"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "22c6899a78214dd841c266348ae997027ef391174ddb21127f1b71dc1b362824"
+    decision: version-bump
+  - root: "event:session/title"
+    previous: "2026-09-11-initial"
+    after: "23adcfe0415603966c200c2af3031af3cc95dea3514c432c42e42ad3aa596331"
+    decision: version-bump
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+V4 provider titles require human message references. V5 additionally accepts provider titles with a matching earlier task binding and no human references. V4-to-V5 retains committed predecessors and emits a validated successor. Old runtimes reject V5; rollback uses backups and does not silently discard later work.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+Native packaged V4-to-V5 publication, source-byte preservation, title search and ownership checks pass. Targeted restoration tests and full Host/Client builds pass; restart and cache checks are recorded in the implementation report.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
