+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Session format V5 enables registered plugin task titles and prevents older runtimes from opening its generations."
+---
+# Plugin task sessions use format V5
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Confirmed plugin tasks can become native historical Sessions without an Agent Loop turn. Their provider-owned titles cite task registration rather than human chat. This changes Session format semantics from V4 to V5; package release versions and the Agent Loop are unchanged. An older runtime refuses V5 even when a V4 predecessor remains.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Save edits and exit the desktop application. Back up the installed application, Harness home and project files before using the repair build.
+2. Install the matching repair build. Opening and writing an old Session creates a verified `session.v5.jsonl` or `session.v5.jsonl.zstd` successor; committed V4 predecessors are preserved. Read-only preparation does not publish a successor.
+3. Open the confirmed ScholarFlow paper. Its authenticated repair operation registers the existing task without generating again. Verify the sidebar name, title search, and restart recovery.
+4. Roll back only with retained backups. Preserve and export newer V5 work first; selecting V4 directly is not a supported downgrade and cannot recover newer changes. Official updates must support V5 before reading these Sessions.
