@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+---
+description: "Streaming V4-to-V5 migration and registered plugin task title validation."
+kind: "package-library"
+---
+# Session format V4 to V5
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+<a id="summary"></a>
+## Summary
+
+Restore released V4 Sessions into V5 while preserving their original generation. This library owns the adjacent conversion and validates titles against earlier confirmed plugin task registrations. Persistence owns publication; the library does not run models or create chat turns.
+
+<a id="table-of-contents"></a>
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [V4 to V5 specification](#v4-to-v5-specification)
+- [Native V5 admission](#native-v5-admission)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+The build-static format catalog imports this library; it is not a mounted plugin. It reuses the frozen V4 source codec and exports the V5 codec, header validator, adjacent migration, and target restorer. Session package versions remain independent of the log format integer.
+
+<a id="v4-to-v5-specification"></a>
+## V4 to V5 specification
+
+Headers change only `version: 4` to `version: 5`. Events retain ids, seq, time, content, references, and inherited cuts. Active `session-log-deepseek/delivery-accepted` markers change `sessionFormatVersion: 4` to `5` without changing coordinates. Older delivery generations remain unchanged. Compact runs are transformed incrementally through their expanded events; no whole-artifact array transformation occurs.
+
+An old ignorable `session/plugin-task-bound` is an external vocabulary collision and becomes `external/v4/session/plugin-task-bound`, with payload and envelope unchanged. A required occurrence is refused. Other opaque ignorable data stays unchanged. Native V5 task-title syntax in V4 input is refused rather than reinterpreted. The target restorer validates all preserved V4 relationships, and publication belongs to the immutable-generation persistence owner. Failed conversion leaves the source intact and publishes no partial successor.
+
+<a id="native-v5-admission"></a>
+## Native V5 admission
+
+A provider title without human message references must include `source.task` with pluginId, projectId, taskId and bindingSeq. Its provider must equal `plugin-task:<pluginId>`. bindingSeq must name a strictly earlier ignorable registration with the same identities; a native registration names the current Session, while an inherited ancestor registration can remain inside its seed cut. Other provider titles still cite human messages; manual titles cite none. Task titles cannot claim model-call metadata. The target restorer uses a validation-only V4 view for unchanged relationships; returned data retains the original provider ownership and V5 delivery generation.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Historical restoration
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+This library makes no model calls and changes no message content, tools, system prompt, or request prefix. `session/plugin-task-bound` and task titles are log-only. Migration retains reconstructed model history.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Conversion changes no token-bearing request text.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The recorded request prefix remains unchanged; provider cache availability is outside this library.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- Older format-v4 runtimes cannot read V5 generations. Rollback requires preserved installation and data backups; it must not silently discard new V5 edits.
+- No runtime invariant companion is published because this pure library owns no independently maintained runtime observations. The persistence owner validates before publication.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+None.
